# jippitese language card

Load this before writing `.jip`; the code compiles under v0. Rust-like, except:
`module a.b` is the first line of every file; paths use `.` (`::` only in
`f::<T>(x)`); a `/// doc` line on every `pub` item; full signatures at
boundaries; effects follow the return type as `with {…}`, omitted when pure
(`io net nondet mut spawn approve llm<role> decide<role>`); closures are
`fn(x) => e`; `var` is a mutable local; no indexing, use `xs.get(i)` (an
`Option`); `+ - *` trap on overflow.

```jip
module orders.billing
use std.json
use std.time
use http                         // dependency alias from app.jip deps {}

/// Money in minor units.
pub type Money(Int)              // newtype: Money(5).0 == 5

/// A customer order.
pub type Order { id: OrderId, lines: List<Line>, total: Money }
  inv total.0 >= 0

/// Why an order could not be billed.
pub enum BillError { NoFunds(Money), Net(http.Error), Declined(Str) }

/// What finance answers on a high-risk order.
pub enum Decision { Proceed, Decline }

/// Sum of line totals.
pub fn total(lines: List<Line>) -> Money {
  Money(lines.map(fn(l) => l.price.0 * l.qty).sum())
}

/// Withdraws amt; Err if funds are insufficient.
pub fn withdraw(acc: Account, amt: Money) -> Result<Account, BillError>
  pre  amt.0 > 0
  post match ret { Ok(a) => a.balance.0 == acc.balance.0 - amt.0, Err(_) => true }
{
  if acc.balance.0 < amt.0 { return Err(NoFunds(amt)) }
  Ok(Account { ..acc, balance: Money(acc.balance.0 - amt.0) })
}

/// Generator for `any Money via positive_money`.
pub fn positive_money(g: Gen) -> Money { Money(g.int(1, 1_000_000)) }

/// Charges the order through the payment gateway.
pub fn charge(o: Order, gw: Gateway) -> Result<Receipt, BillError> with {net, nondet} {
  let resp = http.post(gw.url, json.encode(ChargeReq { order: o.id, amount: o.total }))?  // lifts into Net
  var attempts = 0
  while attempts < 3 && resp.status == 503 { attempts += 1 }
  match json.decode::<Receipt>(resp.body) {
    Ok(r) => Ok(Receipt { ..r, at: time.now() }),
    Err(e) => Err(Declined("bad receipt: {e}")),
  }
}

/// Picks the risk tier with a model; `llm<smart>(prompt, x)` returns Result<T, LlmError>.
pub fn risk(o: Order) -> Tier with {decide<fast>} { decide<fast>(o) }

/// Bills an order durably; finance approves high-risk ones.
impl Workflow for Billing {
  type Input = Order
  type Output = Receipt
  type Signal = Cancel
  type E = BillError
  const version = 2
  fn init(cfg: Config) -> Result<Self, BillError> with {io} { Ok(Billing { gw: Gateway { url: cfg.gateway_url } }) }
  fn run(self, o: Order) -> Result<Receipt, WorkflowError<BillError>> with {net, nondet, decide<fast>, approve} {
    let r = charge(o, self.gw)?                  // journaled step; BillError lifts to App(_)
    if risk(o) != Tier.High { return Ok(r) }
    let review = Review { title: "High-risk order {o.id}", body: "Total {o.total.0}", timeout: Some(48h), data: None }
    match approve::<Decision>(review)? {
      Proceed => Ok(r),
      Decline => Err(WorkflowError.App(Declined("finance declined"))),
    }
  }
}
```

Other behaviours (`Service`, `Worker`, `Cron`, `Repository<T, K>`, `Cache`,
`Agent`, `Machine`) take the same shape; copy one from the project.

Scenarios live in `<module>/scenarios.jip`; clock and randomness are fake:

```jip
module orders.billing.scenarios
use orders.billing

scenario "withdraw never overdraws" {
  given acc = any Account                        // respects `inv`
  given amt = any Money via positive_money
  when  r = withdraw(acc, amt)
  then  match r { Ok(a) => a.balance.0 >= 0, Err(_) => true }
}

scenario "charge sends the order total" {
  given http = FakeHttp.new().reply(200, b"{\"id\":\"r1\",\"amount\":500}")
  given o = Order { id: OrderId(1), lines: [], total: Money(500) }
  when  r = charge(o, Gateway { url: Url("https://pay.test/charge") })
  then  r.is_ok()
  then  http.requests().len() == 1
}
```

`given (a, b) in rows` runs a scenario once per row. Commands: `jip check`
(after changing anything `pub`, docs included: `jip check
--write-interfaces`, plus `--accept-breaking <module>` for a break), `jip
test`, `jip context <module>`, `jip fmt`.

You work through tools: list_dir, read_file, write_file, edit_file, and run, which runs one of `jip check`, `jip context <module>`, `jip test` and `jip fmt` in the project root. `jip context <module>` prints a module's context pack: its public items and what it depends on. When a change alters a module's public interface, run `jip check --write-interfaces`; a deliberately breaking change also needs `--accept-breaking <module>`. The change is done when `jip check` and `jip test` both pass. Hidden acceptance scenarios run after you finish. Finish with a one-line summary.

The indexer in `shop.orders` must also reject an order whose total is
above 100_000, with `IndexError.Rejected("too large")`, so it never counts
towards a customer's total. An order of exactly 100_000 is accepted.

module shop.orders

/// Order `id` was placed by a customer.
pub type Placed { id: Int, customer: Int, total: Int }

/// Why indexing an order failed.
pub enum IndexError { Repo(RepoError), Rejected(Str) }

/// Running order totals per customer, kept in process.
pub type Totals { by_customer: MutMap<Int, Int> }

/// The totals store.
impl Repository<Int, Int> for Totals {
  fn init(cfg: Config) -> Result<Self, RepoError> with {io, mut} {
    Ok(Totals { by_customer: MutMap.new() })
  }
  fn get(self, k: Int) -> Result<Option<Int>, RepoError> with {mut} { Ok(self.by_customer.get(k)) }
  fn put(self, k: Int, v: Int) -> Result<(), RepoError> with {mut} {
    self.by_customer.insert(k, v)
    Ok(())
  }
  fn delete(self, k: Int) -> Result<(), RepoError> with {mut} {
    self.by_customer.remove(k)
    Ok(())
  }
  fn query(self, q: Query<Int>) -> Result<List<Int>, RepoError> with {mut} {
    Ok(self.by_customer.freeze().values())
  }
}

/// The ids of orders already added to a total, kept in process.
pub type Counted { ids: MutMap<Int, Bool> }

/// The counted-orders store.
impl Repository<Bool, Int> for Counted {
  fn init(cfg: Config) -> Result<Self, RepoError> with {io, mut} {
    Ok(Counted { ids: MutMap.new() })
  }
  fn get(self, k: Int) -> Result<Option<Bool>, RepoError> with {mut} { Ok(self.ids.get(k)) }
  fn put(self, k: Int, v: Bool) -> Result<(), RepoError> with {mut} {
    self.ids.insert(k, v)
    Ok(())
  }
  fn delete(self, k: Int) -> Result<(), RepoError> with {mut} {
    self.ids.remove(k)
    Ok(())
  }
  fn query(self, q: Query<Bool>) -> Result<List<Bool>, RepoError> with {mut} {
    Ok(self.ids.freeze().values())
  }
}

/// The indexer: no state of its own.
pub type Indexer {}

/// Adds every placed order to its customer's total, once per order id.
impl Worker for Indexer {
  type Msg = Placed
  type E = IndexError
  const retry = Retry { max: 2, backoff: Backoff.Fixed(10ms) }
  fn init(cfg: Config) -> Result<Self, IndexError> with {io} { Ok(Indexer {}) }
  fn perform(self, m: Placed) -> Result<(), IndexError> with {mut} {
    if m.total < 0 { return Err(IndexError.Rejected("negative total")) }
    if Counted.get(m.id)?.is_some() { return Ok(()) }
    let current = Totals.get(m.customer)?.unwrap_or(0)
    Totals.put(m.customer, current + m.total)?
    Counted.put(m.id, true)?
    Ok(())
  }
}

module shop.orders.scenarios
use shop.orders

scenario "placed orders are totalled per customer" {
  when  r = {
    topics.placed.publish(Placed { id: 1, customer: 7, total: 30 })?
    topics.placed.publish(Placed { id: 2, customer: 7, total: 12 })?
    topics.placed.publish(Placed { id: 3, customer: 8, total: 5 })?
    Totals.get(7)
  }
  then  r == Ok(Some(42))
  then  Totals.get(8) == Ok(Some(5))
}

scenario "a rejected order is dead-lettered and counts nothing" {
  when  r = {
    topics.placed.publish(Placed { id: 4, customer: 9, total: -1 })?
    Totals.get(9)
  }
  then  r == Ok(None)
}

scenario "a redelivered order is counted once" {
  when  r = {
    topics.placed.publish(Placed { id: 5, customer: 10, total: 8 })?
    topics.placed.publish(Placed { id: 5, customer: 10, total: 8 })?
    Totals.get(10)
  }
  then  r == Ok(Some(8))
}

